SEG = "CON"
CAT = "fqConduct"
Q = [
    ("Under the Weapons Act 1990 (Qld), firing a weapon on or across private land needs:",
     "The owner's express consent", ["A neighbour's approval", "A police officer's okay", "A club's written notice to you"],
     "Section 56(2) of the Weapons Act makes it an offence, without reasonable excuse, to discharge a weapon on or across private land without the express consent of the owner."),
    ("Without the owner's consent, a person may carry a weapon on private land only if it:",
     "Cannot readily be fired", ["Is held at port arms", "Has the safety catch on", "Is carried only after dark"],
     "Section 56(3) allows carrying without consent only with a reasonable excuse or if the weapon is unloaded, broken or otherwise cannot be readily discharged. A safety catch alone does not count."),
    ("For the private land rule in s 56 of the Weapons Act, the 'owner' includes:",
     "The occupier", ["Any neighbour", "The local council", "Any licensed shooter"],
     "Section 56(1) defines the owner of private land to include the occupier, so a tenant or manager in occupation can give consent."),
    ("Under s 59 of the Weapons Act, a person under the influence of liquor or a drug must not:",
     "Possess or use a weapon", ["Clean an empty weapon", "Buy a new gun safe", "Renew a licence online"],
     "Section 59 says a person must not have physical possession of, or use, a weapon while under the influence of liquor or a drug."),
    ("Section 58 of the Weapons Act prohibits weapon conduct likely to cause death, injury, property damage or:",
     "Alarm to another person", ["Noise near livestock", "Wear on the firearm", "Loss of spare ammunition"],
     "Section 58 bans conduct with a weapon, without reasonable excuse, likely to cause death or injury, unlawful destruction or damage to property, or alarm to another person."),
    ("For the dangerous conduct offence in s 58 of the Weapons Act, which of these also counts as a weapon?",
     "A laser pointer", ["A torch", "A pair of binoculars", "A rangefinder"],
     "Section 58(1) includes a laser pointer, explosives, slingshots, longbows, spear guns, swords and replicas in the meaning of weapon for this offence."),
    ("Firing a weapon towards a building with reckless disregard for anyone's safety is an offence even if:",
     "No one was endangered", ["The building was empty", "The shooter held a licence", "Only one shot was fired"],
     "Section 56A(2) of the Weapons Act says it is irrelevant whether anyone's safety was in fact endangered by the discharge."),
    ("A buyer who holds a permit to acquire buys a rifle from a private seller. The sale must happen:",
     "Through a licensed dealer", ["At any public car park", "Through a club notice board", "By online payment only"],
     "Sections 35 and 36 of the Weapons Act require acquisition and sale between private people to happen through a licensed dealer, or through a police officer in prescribed circumstances."),
    ("Giving a rifle as a gift to a licensed friend who holds a permit to acquire must happen:",
     "Through a licensed dealer", ["Directly, by hand", "Through their shooting club", "By registered post"],
     "Example 2 to s 35 of the Weapons Act says a gift of a weapon may only be made through a licensed dealer, who must report the acquisition."),
    ("A weapon may be acquired through a police officer instead of a dealer when the nearest dealer is more than:",
     "100 km away", ["25 km away", "50 km away", "200 km away"],
     "Section 102 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 allows this when the nearest licensed dealer is more than 100 km from the person's usual place of residence."),
    ("For a person who does not yet hold a firearm, a permit to acquire cannot be decided until:",
     "28 days after applying", ["7 days after applying", "14 days after applying", "60 days after applying"],
     "Section 101 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 sets the waiting period at 28 days after the application is lodged."),
    ("The permit to acquire waiting period shortens to the same day when the applicant:",
     "Already holds a firearm", ["Has passed a safety course", "Is a member of a club", "Lives far from a dealer"],
     "Under s 101(3) of the Weapons Regulation 2016, the period is the rest of the day of lodging if the applicant already holds a firearm under a licence or there are exceptional circumstances."),
    ("The National Firearms Safety Code says an unwanted firearm should be:",
     "Handed to police or a dealer", ["Buried on rural land", "Given to a relative", "Left at a club range"],
     "Code principle 16 says to dispose of unwanted firearms lawfully: surrender them to police or sell them to or through a licensed dealer, and get a receipt."),
    ("Selling or giving a firearm to a person with no firearm licence is:",
     "An offence", ["Lawful with a receipt", "Lawful for heirlooms", "Lawful between family"],
     "The Code warns that selling or giving a firearm to an unlicensed person is an offence, and s 36 of the Weapons Act limits sales to dealers and permit holders through a dealer."),
    ("A minor aged at least 11 may use a category A or B weapon where it is lawful if directly supervised by:",
     "A licensed parent or guardian", ["Any adult family friend", "An older licensed sibling", "A school sports teacher"],
     "Section 52(1) of the Weapons Act requires direct and immediate supervision by a parent, guardian or person acting in their place who is licensed to possess the weapon."),
    ("An unlicensed adult who wants to try shooting at an approved range must first:",
     "Show photo ID and sign a form", ["Pass a written test", "Buy a permit to acquire", "Show a club membership card"],
     "Section 53(2) of the Weapons Act requires the person to show photographic identification to a range officer and complete and sign the approved form before using the weapon."),
    ("While an unlicensed person uses a weapon at an approved range, a range officer must:",
     "Supervise them at all times", ["Check on them every hour", "Load the weapon for them", "Keep their licence card"],
     "Section 53(5) of the Weapons Act requires the range officer, or another range officer, to supervise the person at all times while they physically possess the weapon."),
    ("A person attending an approved range must comply with:",
     "A range officer's directions", ["Other shooters' wishes", "The range booking terms only", "Their own judgment alone"],
     "Section 110(3) of the Weapons Act requires a person at an approved range to comply with a range officer's direction given for the Act or safety reasons, unless they have a reasonable excuse."),
    ("An experienced minor may be supervised at a range in a group. The most minors one supervisor may watch at once is:",
     "6", ["3", "10", "12"],
     "Section 38 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 allows a range officer or appointee to supervise no more than 6 such minors at the same time."),
    ("To be supervised as an experienced minor at a range, a minor must have fired at an approved range on at least:",
     "3 separate occasions", ["2 separate occasions", "5 separate occasions", "10 separate occasions"],
     "Section 38(1)(a) of the Weapons Regulation 2016 requires the minor to have fired a weapon at an approved range on at least 3 separate occasions."),
    ("A range officer supervising an approved range must take all reasonable steps to ensure:",
     "Attendees obey the Act", ["Every shooter scores well", "The range makes a profit", "Each target is replaced"],
     "Section 109 of the Weapons Act makes the range officer responsible for taking all reasonable steps to ensure people attending the range do not contravene the Act."),
    ("A licensee at an approved range may use a firearm only if the range officer permits it and it is:",
     "Of an approved category", ["Fitted with a telescopic sight", "Their only registered firearm", "Loaded before arriving"],
     "Section 110(1) of the Weapons Act requires possession or use to be permitted by the range officer and to comply with the range's approval conditions, such as the categories of weapon allowed."),
    ("Unless specially endorsed, which handgun may a Queensland minor's licence holder not possess?",
     "One over .38 inch calibre", ["A .22 rim-fire pistol", "A target air pistol", "A black-powder pistol"],
     "Section 37 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 bars category H weapons over .38 inch calibre, unless endorsed for an accredited event. Black-powder pistols are excluded from that rule."),
    ("Under the Weapons Act, a landowner who gives a shooter written permission to shoot on their land:",
     "Is not liable just for that", ["Becomes liable for any injury", "Must supervise every shot", "Must hold a licence too"],
     "Section 168 of the Weapons Act says a landowner does not incur any liability merely because they provide written permission to shoot on their land."),
]
